From 2a83ae3e1902efdb5d0e4baaf50f3de9c65495bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 72/77] test: add OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S script tests and signature
 message vectors

The rows are written in C++, in p2mr_slhdsa128s_tests, and signed there
with the vendored library rather than kept in script_tests.json: a
signature is 7.9 KB, and the unit tests sign over the messages the
interpreter computes. Every spend is checked with the plain checker,
through DeferringSignatureChecker, and with the caching checker of block
validation, which must agree.

- The parameters: Ark-0 does not activate the rules at any height,
  ARK0_SLHDSA128S_HEIGHT is std::numeric_limits<int>::max() (setting it
  at release changes this test on purpose), other signets and the public
  chains never activate them, regtest does from genesis or where
  -testactivationheight says, and -signetslhdsa128s with every way it is
  refused.
- The signature messages of 11 cases, against those of the functional
  test framework for key_version 0, 1 and 2, in leaf versions 0xc0 and
  0xe0 (test/util/generate_p2mr_slhdsa128s_sighash.py writes them).
- Valid spends in leaf versions 0xc0 and 0xe0, with disabled elliptic
  curve checks too, and with each of the six hash types; a committed
  annex; a check after OP_CODESEPARATOR.
- Failures: a signature for the other leaf version, another hash type
  byte, another annex or none, key_version 0, 1 and 3, the empty context
  string and those of M1 and M4-B, the internal interface and
  HashSLH-DSA, a flipped bit in each part of the signature, PK.seed or
  PK.root changed; the stack, chunk, key and hash type rules and the
  order in which they are checked; sixteen empty chunks push false, and
  OP_NOT turns that into true but not an invalid signature.
- The validation weight: a leaf whose budget its checks use up exactly
  passes, one byte of witness less fails, and empty signatures use none.
  The number of checks and the padding follow from
  VALIDATION_WEIGHT_PER_SLHDSA128S_CHECK, so that the provisional value
  can change without touching the test.
- Where the byte is not the opcode: before activation, in P2TR, in
  legacy and witness v0 scripts, at depth zero, inside pushed data, next
  to another OP_SUCCESSx, in a branch that does not execute.
- The cache entries, apart from those of ML-DSA-44, and a hit that does
  not call the library; the relay template.
